---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Summary from '../components/Summary.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
---
<Base title={"Autism Therapy in Utah | Tangible Therapy"} description={"Autism therapy for teens & adults in Provo, Orem, & Sandy, Utah. Neurodiversity-affirming care that helps you thrive without masking. Free 15-min consult."}>
<section class="sec t-black h-medium has-bg has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-bg"><img src="/images/tangible-31-e8444f.jpg" alt="A therapist and client in a calm conversation in a bright office with tall plants at Tangible Therapy in Utah" style="object-position:50% 50%" loading="eager"><div class="sec-ov" style="opacity:0.5"></div></div><div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:7;--mrows:10">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/5/6/23;--m:1/2/7/10"><div class="rte"><h1 class="ta-center">Autism Therapy</h1><p class="lg ta-center">Autism therapy that honors who you are and helps you thrive on your terms</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:6/11/8/18;--m:7/2/9/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="https://tangible.clientsecure.me/">Start Autism-Informed Therapy Today</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#fff" /></section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:12;--mrows:21">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/16/12/26;--m:13/2/21/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:40px"><img src="/images/autism-therapist-bcd22a.jpg" alt="Autism Therapist and adult female client in a comfortable therapy session at Tangible Therapy&#x27;s autism therapy clinic in Orem Utah" width="2203" height="1702" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:3/2/6/12;--m:2/2/5/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>Therapy that supports you, where you are</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/2/10/12;--m:5/2/13/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>For individuals with autism, navigating a world built for neurotypical people can be exhausting, overwhelming, or isolating. Whether you’ve been diagnosed recently or have known for years, therapy can help you understand yourself better, reduce stress, and build the life you want, without forcing you to mask or conform.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:17;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/2/17/13;--m:13/2/20/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:40px"><img src="/images/tangible-33-16b0c5.jpg" alt="Neurodiversity-affirming therapist offering autism support to a client in Provo, Utah" width="2500" height="1932" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/14/5/25;--m:2/2/5/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>What autism-informed therapy looks like</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/14/17/25;--m:5/2/13/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>At Tangible Therapy, we offer neurodiversity-affirming care. That means we don’t try to “fix” you or force strategies that go against your natural way of thinking or being.&nbsp;</p><p>Instead, we work with you to identify what supports your well-being: socially, emotionally, and practically.</p><p>We offer therapy for:</p><ul><li><p>Autistic adults and teens</p></li><li><p>Late-diagnosed or self-identified individuals</p></li><li><p>Autistic people with co-occurring conditions like anxiety, OCD, or ADHD</p></li><li><p>Burnout and masking fatigue</p></li><li><p>Support with social, sensory, and communication challenges</p></li><li><p>Emotional regulation and self-advocacy</p></li></ul></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:12;--mrows:21">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/16/12/26;--m:14/2/21/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:40px"><img src="/images/autism-therapist-at-tangible-58f82d.jpg" alt="Evidence-based autism therapy session at Tangible Therapy in Utah County" width="2500" height="1719" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:3/2/5/12;--m:2/2/5/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>You don’t have to do it all alone</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/2/9/12;--m:5/2/11/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>Life can feel confusing, especially when you’ve been trying to fit into boxes that don’t suit you. Whether you're facing sensory overload, struggling to connect with others, or learning to embrace your identity, we’re here to help you feel more grounded, capable, and understood.</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:9/2/11/7;--m:11/2/13/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="https://tangible.clientsecure.me/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book Your Session</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-in" style="padding-top:6.6vmax;padding-bottom:6.6vmax">
<div class="wrap"><div class="list-title rte"><p>What you’ll get</p></div><ul class="ulist ulist-carousel" style="--per:3;--ar:3/2;--tfs:calc((2.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--bfs:calc((1.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--cw:75%;--gap:20px"><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="#" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Process and unmask safely, without judgment</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Navigate relationships, routines, or life transitions</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Develop tools for emotional regulation</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Build confidence in communication and boundaries</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Strengthen identity and self-understanding</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="/" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Recover from burnout and reestablish balance</p></div></div></li></ul><div class="carousel-nav"><button class="prev" aria-label="Previous"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 12H5m6-6-6 6 6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button><button class="next" aria-label="Next"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button></div></div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#565d57" /></section>

<section class="sec t-light h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:16;--mrows:7">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/7/3/22;--m:1/2/3/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">Autism Affirming Therapists</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-summary-v2" style="--d:3/5/17/24;--m:3/2/8/10"><Summary kind="team" design="carousel" category="telehealth/autism" limit={9} perRow={3} rounded /></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/4/26;--m:1/2/4/10"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">✺ Frequently asked questions ✺</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/2/14/13;--m:5/2/13/10"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>Do I need an official autism diagnosis to work with you?</summary><div class="rte"><p>No. We welcome late-diagnosed, self-diagnosed, and questioning individuals. You don’t need a formal label to seek support that feels right.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is this therapy only for kids or teens?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Not at all. We specialize in working with autistic teens <em>and</em> adults. Many of our clients were diagnosed in adulthood or are exploring neurodivergence for the first time.</p></div></details><details><summary>Will you try to make me act more “neurotypical”?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Absolutely not. Our approach is neurodiversity-affirming — we support your strengths and help you work through challenges without asking you to mask or change who you are.</p></div></details></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/15/10/26;--m:13/2/21/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>What if I have other diagnoses too?</summary><div class="rte"><p>That’s very common. Many autistic people also experience anxiety, OCD, ADHD, depression, or trauma. We’re trained to work with overlapping needs and will tailor therapy accordingly.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I bring tools, stims, or sensory items to the session?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Yes. You’re encouraged to show up as you are. We welcome fidgets, headphones, scripts, weighted items — whatever helps you feel comfortable and supported.</p></div></details></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</Base>
